I want you to work ONLY on the HOME PAGE of this project.

IMPORTANT: Do not redesign, modify, restructure, or add functionality to any other page or tab in this task.

The only things you are allowed to modify are:
1. The Home page.
2. The Settings interface opened from the Home page.
3. The specific underlying logic required to make Home-page features function correctly.

Do not work on the Play/Tower page, Shop, Achievements, Leaderboard, Lessons page, Battle system, or any other page.

Before making changes, inspect the existing project and understand how the current Home page and its data/functionality work.

==================================================
1. HOME PAGE — OVERALL GOAL
==================================================

The Home page should feel like the main dashboard of a real educational game.

It should communicate the player's current status and give them a clear reason to continue playing.

The Home page should contain the following core information/features:

- Player name
- Player level / XP progression
- Coins
- Current streak
- Current league
- Continue Your Journey
- Tower progression preview
- Word of the Day
- Lucky Wheel
- Robo Specter

Do not turn the page into a cluttered dashboard.

The player should immediately understand:

"Who am I?"
"How am I progressing?"
"What should I do next?"
"What rewards/features can I interact with today?"

==================================================
2. TOP PLAYER STATUS
==================================================

Keep the player's name and progression clearly visible near the top.

Display:

- Player name
- XP / level progression
- Coins
- Streak
- League

These elements should look like part of one coherent game HUD/status area rather than unrelated cards.

The league should remain visible because it is part of the player's progression and motivation.

Do not invent a new league system.

Use the existing league/progression logic if it already exists.

==================================================
3. SETTINGS BUTTON
==================================================

Move the Settings gear to a proper corner position.

It should be located where users naturally expect a settings button to be, rather than floating awkwardly inside the page content.

It should remain visually secondary to the main gameplay/progression elements.

When opened, redesign the Settings interface so it looks polished and consistent with the rest of the game.

Keep the useful existing settings, such as:

- Dark/Light mode
- Language
- Logout
- Close

Remove the option to change the player's learning stage/grade from Settings.

The learning stage should not be casually changed from this menu.

Do not invent unnecessary settings.

The Settings interface should be simple, clean, and game-like.

==================================================
4. ROBOSPECTER
==================================================

Robo Specter should appear ABOVE "Continue Your Journey."

He should feel like an actual guide/companion in the game rather than a decorative message at the bottom of the homepage.

His messages should be short and contextual.

He can comment on things such as:

- The player's current progress
- What the player should do next
- A useful tip
- A small piece of lore
- A player's recent accomplishment
- Encouragement

Do not make Robo Specter dominate the screen.

The player should understand that he is part of the game's world.

Use the existing Robo Specter implementation where possible rather than creating a completely separate system.

==================================================
5. CONTINUE YOUR JOURNEY
==================================================

"Continue Your Journey" should be the primary call-to-action on the Home page.

It should clearly tell the player what they are continuing.

For example:

"Continue Lesson 1"

or

"Continue Lesson 7"

depending on the player's actual progress.

This must be dynamic.

Do NOT hardcode one lesson.

When the player presses it, it should continue the player's current journey using the existing lesson/navigation system.

IMPORTANT:

Do NOT redesign the Lessons page in this task.

Do NOT create a Lessons tab.

Do NOT create a large lesson-progress section on the Home page.

The Home page only needs one clear gateway into the player's current lesson:

CONTINUE YOUR JOURNEY.

==================================================
6. TOWER PROGRESSION PREVIEW
==================================================

Keep the Tower progression preview on the Home page.

This is ONLY a preview of the player's Tower progression.

Do NOT move the actual Tower onto the Home page.

Do NOT redesign the Tower page.

The Home page preview should communicate the player's progression through the Tower at a glance.

It should show things such as:

- Current Tower progression
- Current level/floor
- Previously completed/explored progression
- Current position

The existing visual language can be improved, but do not turn this into a full Tower map.

If the existing preview is clickable, preserve that functionality.

==================================================
7. WORD OF THE DAY
==================================================

Keep Word of the Day on the Home page.

It should be a daily feature.

It should be accessible directly from the Home page.

Do not create duplicate Word of the Day components.

Use the existing Word of the Day logic if it already exists.

Do not lock Word of the Day behind an unrelated boss or progression requirement unless there is an explicit technical reason that already exists in the project.

If there is an unnecessary lock, identify and remove it.

The feature should clearly communicate that it is a daily activity.

==================================================
8. LUCKY WHEEL
==================================================

The Lucky Wheel needs to feel like an actual interactive game feature.

Currently, the problem is that the wheel does not properly spin and can appear to simply produce a reward without showing the player the actual spinning process.

Fix this.

When the player activates the Lucky Wheel:

1. The wheel visibly rotates.
2. It rotates for a short, satisfying amount of time.
3. It gradually slows down.
4. It stops on a reward.
5. The selected reward is clearly revealed.
6. The player receives the reward exactly once.
7. The button cannot accidentally trigger multiple spins while the wheel is already spinning.

Do NOT simply display a reward immediately after the player clicks.

The player needs to SEE the wheel spin.

If reward-selection logic already exists, preserve it and connect the animation to the existing reward logic rather than creating a duplicate reward system.

The Lucky Wheel should feel like a small but satisfying game interaction.

==================================================
9. INITIAL TUTORIAL / ONBOARDING
==================================================

Fix the existing homepage tutorial so that it does not trap the player.

The tutorial should guide the player through the Home page step by step.

The player should NOT need to refresh the page to regain control.

The tutorial should:

1. Highlight the intended element.
2. Prevent unrelated interaction only while that tutorial step is active.
3. Allow the player to click/tap the highlighted element.
4. Advance to the next tutorial step.
5. Finish cleanly.
6. Restore normal Home-page interaction.

It must work with both:

- Desktop mouse/click interaction
- Mobile touch interaction

Do not leave the player stuck on the tutorial.

Do not require a browser refresh.

==================================================
10. LESSON DATA CHECK
==================================================

Inspect the actual lesson data in the project.

The intended structure is 30 lessons for each learning stage/grade that the application supports.

Do NOT blindly assume the project already contains exactly 30 lessons.

Actually inspect the data.

Determine:

- How many lessons currently exist.
- How they are grouped by learning stage/grade.
- Whether each intended learning stage/grade contains 30 lessons.
- Whether anything is missing.
- Whether anything is duplicated.
- Whether the Home page progression is using actual lesson data or hardcoded numbers.

If the lesson structure is incorrect, fix the underlying data only if doing so is safe and does not require inventing educational content.

If educational content is missing, do NOT fabricate lessons.

Instead, report exactly what exists and what is missing.

The important requirement is that the Home page must use the actual lesson progression data rather than hardcoded lesson numbers.

==================================================
11. VISUAL DESIGN
==================================================

The current design is already moving in a better direction.

Improve it rather than completely replacing it.

The result should feel like a real game.

Use:

- Strong visual hierarchy
- Clear primary CTA
- Consistent cards
- Good spacing
- Clear progression indicators
- Subtle animations
- Touch feedback
- Hover feedback where appropriate
- Consistent typography
- Consistent visual language

Avoid:

- Excessive emojis as game assets
- Random decorative elements
- Duplicate features
- Too many competing buttons
- Large empty spaces
- A generic educational-dashboard appearance

I will provide better custom game assets later.

Therefore, structure the implementation so that icons/assets can easily be replaced later without rebuilding the entire Home page.

Do not spend this task replacing every existing asset.

==================================================
12. EXISTING NAVIGATION
==================================================

Preserve the existing navigation structure.

Do not add, remove, rename, or rearrange navigation tabs during this task.

Do not create a new Lessons navigation tab.

Do not create new navigation destinations.

The purpose of this task is to improve the existing Home page, not redesign the application's navigation architecture.

==================================================
13. IMPORTANT SCOPE RESTRICTION
==================================================

THIS IS A HOMEPAGE-ONLY TASK.

Do not redesign or modify:

- Play/Tower page
- Shop
- Achievements
- Leaderboard
- Lessons page
- Battle system
- Any other page

Do not "improve" unrelated parts of the application simply because you notice something that could be improved.

If you notice an unrelated problem, leave it alone.

Only make changes outside the Home page if a minimal technical change is absolutely required for a Home-page feature to function correctly.

==================================================
14. IMPLEMENTATION PROCESS
==================================================

Before editing:

1. Inspect the project structure.
2. Identify the Home-page components/files.
3. Identify the data/state used by:
   - XP
   - Level
   - Coins
   - Streak
   - League
   - Tower progression
   - Word of the Day
   - Lucky Wheel
   - Robo Specter
   - Continue Your Journey
   - Tutorial/onboarding
4. Check for duplicate components.
5. Check for duplicate Word of the Day or Lucky Wheel implementations.
6. Check whether any Home-page features are incorrectly locked.
7. Check the lesson data structure.
8. Make a short implementation plan.
9. Then implement the changes.

After implementation:

1. Verify the Home page renders correctly.
2. Verify the Settings interface works.
3. Verify the Lucky Wheel actually animates and spins.
4. Verify the reward is granted exactly once.
5. Verify Word of the Day works.
6. Verify Continue Your Journey works.
7. Verify the tutorial can be completed without refreshing.
8. Verify desktop interaction.
9. Verify mobile/touch interaction.
10. Verify XP, coins, streak, league, and progression display correctly.
11. Verify there are no duplicate Home-page features.
12. Verify that unrelated pages were not redesigned or changed unnecessarily.

Do not stop after changing the visual appearance.

Actually verify the interactions.

If something cannot safely be implemented because of the current architecture, explain the exact technical limitation instead of creating a fake or disconnected implementation.

==================================================
